# Windows cache cleaner

Builds a guarded cleanup plan for regenerable Windows, application, package,
browser, and development-tool caches.

In the TUI, the first run is always a preview. Nothing is deleted until that
preview finishes successfully and you type `CLEAN`. Apply repeats discovery
with the same settings, so targets may change between the two runs.

## What it can clean

- current-user temporary, Direct3D, Internet, and app `TempState` caches
- Edge, Chrome, Brave, Chromium, and Firefox caches
- Chocolatey, Scoop, and NuGet caches
- Delivery Optimization and the Windows component store in system mode

## Safety

Normal cleanup runs without elevation. System cleanup is deliberately separate
and requires an elevated 64-bit PowerShell process. The script validates local
fixed-drive paths, refuses protected paths, and does not follow reparse points.

Close browsers, packaged apps, and development tools before applying the plan.

## Options

| Option | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `-AllTemp` | include recent current-user temp files |
| `-System` | run the separate elevated Windows cleanup |
| `-GlobalPackages` | clear the global NuGet package folder |
| `-Verbose` | print every filesystem target |
| `-Apply` | repeat discovery with deletion enabled |
| `-Yes` | accept the script's prompt after TUI confirmation |

## Direct CLI

```powershell
sys\windows\clean.ps1
sys\windows\clean.ps1 -Verbose
sys\windows\clean.ps1 -Apply
```
